ifferent single-center buffer and cannot absorb the propane qualifier. All three frozen occurrences retain2.25g/L and the same explicit buffer identity. Evidence and exact frozen scope are recorded in reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/fragments/chemistry-decisions.json. This proposed delta does not approve complete owner/export payload or remove inherited holds.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Bis_Tris_Propane.after.yaml:13:- synonym_text: Bis Tris Propane\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Bis_Tris_Propane.after.yaml:22:  changes: 'Isolated source-review proposal bis-tris-propane: new exact ingredient identity; added aliases [''Bis Tris Propane'']; rejected provenance labels [] Subject to independent skeptical review and guarded coordinator integration; inherited full-payload support must not transfer.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/TAPS_Sodium_Salt.after.yaml:5:  ontology_label: N-[tris(hydroxymethyl)methyl]-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/TAPS_Sodium_Salt.after.yaml:17:    notes: 'narrowMatch parent CHEBI:26714 (''sodium salt'') -> CHEBI:191055 (''N-[tris(hydroxymethyl)methyl]-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid''). The previous parent was the class of all sodium salts: it retained the counterion and discarded the compound, collapsing unrelated ingredients onto one node. Chosen because it is the systematic name of TAPS. The record stays cas-primary per MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 step 2; only the parent moves.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/TAPS_Sodium_Salt.after.yaml:67:  changes: ontology_mapping CHEBI:26714 'sodium salt' -> CHEBI:191055 'N-[tris(hydroxymethyl)methyl]-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid' (#322); the systematic name of TAPS.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/biological/JCM_512_DL_Minerals.yaml:18:- component_name: Nitrilotriacetic acid, trisodium salt\ndata/ingredient